Year = {2008},
Volume = {14},
Number = {4},
Pages = {715-740},
Abstract = {This article examines the gender quotas in Belgian parties. In the 2006
   municipal elections many more local party sections had implemented such
   measures than in the preceding elections in 2000, which indicates a
   tendency to integrate the notion of equality. However, the local
   sections exhibit less enthusiasm when it comes to quotas improving the
   gender balance in higher party offices. Our analysis shows that local
   sections have more offices at their disposal are more likely to
   implement quotas. Quotas are accepted more easily when equality is an
   important issue within the party's respective ideology, or when the way
   towards equality has already been paved by women.},
